Tagged KNOWNBUG 2026-07-23 (first full libc++ suite run):
libc++ <set>: "invalid initializer '__pair1_'" in __tree
(mem-initializer naming a member of a compressed-pair base;
__tree line 1341).
Update 2026-07-28: the comparator null-deref is downstream of the
bodyless-member family -- a single insert already shows "no body for
callee __tree::__emplace_unique_key_args / __end_node / ~__tree"
(same class as cpp11_tuple_leaf_no_body, which is the minimal
reproducer for lost member bodies).  A dedicated header-free
reduction is blocked: preprocessed-libc++ sources hit the
cpp20_views_take_call_crash invariant before conversion.  Needs
--object-bits 12 to get past "too many addressed objects".
Masking crash isolated: cpp20_extern_template_copy_ctor_abort.
Update 2026-07-30: the "masking crash" on preprocessed sources was a
MODE artifact (clang builtins lex only under --stdlib libc++); re-fed
preprocessed source with the right flags reproduces the SEMANTIC
failure directly, so header-free reduction is unblocked.
